- insertRatingCheck(publicationId(Long, nullable), channelId, businessDay, segmentId, assetId, rating, windowId(Long), windowMaxRating(Rating), verdict, createdAtMs)
- findRatingChecks(channelId, businessDay) → List ordered by id
- insertBreakin(channelId, assetId, atMs, requestId, createdAtMs) → id

For nullable Long params in jdbc.update: passing null Long works with jdbc.update(sql, args...) — type inference may need Types; PreparedStatementSetter with null works via setObject. Spring's jdbc.update with varargs handles null by setNull with UNKNOWN type — usually fine for H2/MySQL. To be safe use SqlTypeValue? Keep simple: use varargs; H2 handles null fine.

